  "id": "DrugBank_DB01112 - MONDO_1080",
  "verbalization": "Cefuroxime is implicated in the pathogenesis of Acute Gonococcal Cervicitis through a chain of indications that link it to Gonorrhea and subsequently to Acute Gonococcal Cervicitis. The evidence suggests that Cefuroxime is used to treat Gonorrhea, which is a primary cause of Acute Gonococcal Cervicitis. This relationship is further supported by the indication of Cefuroxime in Acute Gonococcal Endometritis, which in turn is linked to Cefoxitin, and Cefoxitin is also linked to Acute Gonococcal Cervicitis. The cumulative evidence indicates that Cefuroxime may play a role in the treatment of gonococcal infections, which can lead to the development of Acute Gonococcal Cervicitis. The mechanisms are not fully elucidated, but the indirect pathways suggest a potential role of Cefuroxime in the pathophysiology of this condition.",
